@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
    ViewData["Description"] = "How Recall.nu handles your data: what we store, the cookies "
        + "we use, how long things are kept, and how passwordless email sign-in works.";
    ViewData["Robots"] = "index, follow";
}
<div class="tvdb-shell tvdb-shell--narrow tvdb-text-page">
    <h1 class="mb-3">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        Recall.nu is a tracker for TV series and movies. We store what is needed to run your
        account: your email address, your username, and the series, movies, watched episodes,
        likes and ratings you add. We don't sell this or use it for advertising, and the site
        has no analytics or tracking scripts.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies">Cookies</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        Recall only uses cookies that are strictly necessary for the site to work, which is why
        you are not asked for consent to them. None is used for tracking, analytics or
        advertising, and nothing else is stored in your browser.
    </p>
    <ul class="tvdb-prose tvdb-privacy-list">
        <li>
            <strong>Sign-in cookie</strong> (<code>@Model.SignInCookieName</code>): keeps you signed in. Set when you
            sign in, renewed as you use the site, and gone after @Model.SignInCookieDays days without a visit or
            when you sign out.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Form protection cookie</strong> (<code>.AspNetCore.Antiforgery</code>): proves that a form was
            sent from this site and not from somewhere else. Set on pages with a form, and removed
            when you close the browser.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Message cookie</strong> (<code>.AspNetCore.Mvc.CookieTempDataProvider</code>): carries a
            confirmation such as "Marked as watched" from one page to the next. It exists for a
            moment and is removed as soon as the message has been shown.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What is loaded from elsewhere</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        Fonts, icons, styles and scripts are served from Recall.nu itself. Two things are not:
    </p>
    <ul class="tvdb-prose tvdb-privacy-list">
        <li>
            <strong>Posters and stills</strong> are loaded by your browser from TheTVDB's image servers
            (<code>artworks.thetvdb.com</code>), which therefore see your IP address, as any website you visit does.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>The sign-in page</strong> may load Cloudflare Turnstile to tell people from bots. When it
            does, your browser talks to Cloudflare, which may set its own cookies for that check.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Sign-in</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        There are no passwords. You enter your email address and we send you a link that works
        once and expires after @Model.SignInLinkMinutes minutes. Once the email has gone out we keep only
        a fingerprint (hash) of the link, not the link itself. Requests for links are rate limited to stop abuse.
    </p>

    <h2 id="emails">Emails</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        We send two kinds of email, and nothing else.
    </p>
    <ul class="tvdb-prose tvdb-privacy-list">
        <li>
            <strong>Sign-in links</strong>, when you ask for one.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>The weekly email</strong>, only if you turn it on (in your profile, or when the Dashboard
            offers it; it is off until you do). It lists new seasons, episodes that aired in the past week
            and that you have not watched, and what airs in the coming week. Weeks with nothing to say
            are skipped.
        </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        You can turn the weekly email off in your profile, or with the link at the bottom of every one,
        which works without signing in. The emails contain no images, no tracking pixels and no tracked
        links: every link goes straight to Recall.nu. We store whether the weekly email is on (and when you
        turned it on), whether you answered the Dashboard's one-time offer, and a record of the weeks we
        have sent it to you so that nobody gets it twice.
    </p>

    <h2 id="stats">Your watch history and stats</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        When you mark an episode or a movie as watched we store which one, when you marked it, and how it
        was marked: one at a time, several at once (a whole season, or an episode together with the earlier
        ones), or by an IMDb import. The time is when you marked it, which is not always when you watched it;
        that is why your stats page leaves anything marked several at once or imported out of its
        month-by-month chart while still counting it in your totals. If you tell us you have stopped watching
        a series, your library records when you did, until you resume it.
    </p>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        Your stats page is worked out from your own watch history and ratings each time you open it.
        Only you can see it: there are no public profiles, and nothing on it is shared or sent anywhere.
    </p>

    <h2>How long things are kept</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        Your library, watch history, likes and ratings are kept for as long as your account
        exists; <a href="#delete">deleting your account</a> removes them. The rest is cleaned up
        automatically once a day:
    </p>
    <ul class="tvdb-prose tvdb-privacy-list">
        <li>Sign-in links: @PrivacyModel.After(Model.Retention.LoginTokenDays, "they expired or were used").</li>
        <li>
            Emails we sent you: the text is erased as soon as the message is delivered; the record that it
            was sent is @PrivacyModel.After(Model.Retention.EmailDays, "sending").
        </li>
        <li>
            Notifications: @PrivacyModel.After(Model.Retention.ReadNotificationDays, "you read them"). Unread
            notifications are kept.
        </li>
        <li>
            The record of which new episodes you have already been told about:
            @PrivacyModel.After(Model.Retention.NotifiedEpisodeDays, "it was made").
        </li>
        <li>IMDb imports and their rows: @PrivacyModel.After(Model.Retention.ImportJobDays, "the import finished").</li>
        <li>The record of which weeks the weekly email was sent to you: @PrivacyModel.After(Model.Retention.DigestLedgerDays, "it was made").</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="delete">Deleting your account</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        You can delete your account yourself: open your
        <a asp-page="/Account/Profile">profile</a> and choose "Delete my account" at the bottom of
        the Account section. You are asked to type your username to confirm.
    </p>
    <ul class="tvdb-prose tvdb-privacy-list">
        <li>
            <strong>Removed immediately:</strong> the account itself (email address and username), your
            library, watch history, likes, ratings, notifications, IMDb imports, sign-in links,
            the emails we sent you, and your weekly-email setting with its history. Ratings you gave no longer count towards Recall ratings.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Not removed immediately:</strong> database backups are kept for about 9 days@(Model.LogRetentionDays is { } days ? $", and server logs for {days} days" : ", and server logs for a limited time").
            Your data disappears from those as they expire. Backups are only used to restore the
            service after a failure.
        </li>
        <li>
            Other browsers where you were signed in stop working within a few minutes. Signing in
            again with the same email address creates a new, empty account.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Logs</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        The server keeps technical logs for operation and security. They can contain IP
        addresses, for example when a rate limit is hit. Logs are not used to profile
        visitors.
        @if (Model.LogRetentionDays is { } logDays)
        {
            <text>Log files are deleted after @logDays days.</text>
        }
    </p>

    <h2>Contact &amp; support</h2>
    <p class="tvdb-prose">
        Questions about your data, a bug to report, or general feedback? Reach us through
        the
        <a href="https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61594107509642" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Recall
        Facebook page</a> and we'll get back to you.
    </p>
</div>
